# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# This file is SECURITY-CRITICAL, not merely a build-speed optimisation. Two
# entries below keep live secrets out of the image layers, and a layer is
# forever: `docker history` and any registry that receives a push can read it
# back even if a later layer deletes the file.
#
#   - .env*        holds the real Intellicar credentials and
#                  CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY. Next.js also loads .env.local
#                  automatically in production, so a copy inside the image would
#                  additionally SHADOW the values Railway injects — a stale
#                  password silently winning over the configured one.
#   - .sessions/   holds an encrypted Playwright storageState. A stored
#                  storageState IS a live session, equivalent to a bearer token
#                  for the customer's fleet portal (see src/services/session/
#                  session-store.ts). It is gitignored for exactly this reason
#                  and must never be baked into an image either.
#
# Everything else here is about build context size. node_modules is 865 MB and
# .next is 214 MB on a working checkout; both are rebuilt inside the image, so
# shipping them would triple the upload for no benefit — and a host-built
# node_modules carries the WRONG platform binaries (Windows lightningcss, for
# instance) into a Linux image.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and live session material — never ship these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
.sessions/

# Playwright diagnostics: failure screenshots, traces, downloads. May contain
# customer dashboard content.
auth-artifacts/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rebuilt inside the image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/

# Prisma client is regenerated in the builder stage (`npx prisma generate`), so
# the host copy must not be carried in: it would be overwritten anyway, and a
# stale one is a confusing failure if generation is ever skipped.
src/generated/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed at build or runtime.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/

# Telemetry datasets are imported manually into PostgreSQL (docs/DATA-IMPORT.md).
# They are not application inputs and never belong in the image.
data/

# Documentation and its media. The runbook is read from the repository, not from
# inside a running container.
docs/
README.md
CLAUDE.md
*.docx

# Local deployment tooling — the compose file describes how to RUN the image, so
# it has no business being INSIDE it.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# TypeScript / tooling caches.
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.eslintcache

# OS and editor noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
